      <div class="eda-analysis-box">
        <div id="awDesc" class="eda-desc">
          <strong>Lane Scaling Mechanics:</strong> Scaling from 1 lane to 4 lanes (Ara) or 8 lanes (AraXL) multiplies spatial arithmetic capacity without increasing instruction-fetch bandwidth. A single <code>vfmacc.vv</code> issued by the host CPU drives all active lanes simultaneously, executing identical micro-operations on independent element slices.
        </div>
        <div id="awTradeoff" class="eda-tradeoff">
          <strong>Silicon Trade-off:</strong> Datapath area grows linearly with lane count (~45 kGE per lane), while memory crossbar routing complexity and area grow as \(O(N^2)\). Without clustered multi-banked VRFs (such as AraXL), wide lane crossbars rapidly become timing critical paths.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

