    <h2 class="block-title">7. First-Class Architectural Dossiers: Open-Source Vector &amp; Coprocessor Engines</h2>
    <p class="block-lead">
      Deep-dive microarchitectural dossiers for all nine evaluated hardware platforms, documenting pipeline stages, memory bus widths, verification evidence, notable strengths, and physical synthesis characteristics:
    </p>

    <!-- DOSSIER 1: ARA -->
    <div id="core-ara" class="core-dossier-card">
      <div class="dossier-header">
        <div class="dossier-badge-row">
          <span class="badge badge-yellow">ARCHETYPE 3</span>
          <span class="badge badge-green">VERIFIED RVV 1.0</span>
          <span class="badge badge-blue">GF 22FDX SILICON</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="dossier-title">Ara &bull; Scalable 4&ndash;16 Lane RVV 1.0 Coprocessor</h3>
        <span class="dossier-sub">ETH Zurich &amp; University of Bologna &bull; Apache-2.0 &bull; SystemVerilog</span>
      </div>

      <div class="dossier-specs-grid">
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">ISA:</span><span class="s-v">RV64GCV (Vector 1.0 Compliant)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Lanes:</span><span class="s-v">4 to 16 Parallel SIMD Lanes</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Vector Length:</span><span class="s-v">512 to 4096 bits (VLEN)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">VRF Banking:</span><span class="s-v">8 SRAM Banks per Lane</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Memory Interface:</span><span class="s-v">128-bit to 512-bit AXI4 Crossbar</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Physical Area:</span><span class="s-v">~220 kGE (4 Lanes) / ~850 kGE (16 Lanes)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Clock Frequency:</span><span class="s-v">1.05 GHz @ 0.8V (GF 22FDX)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Verification:</span><span class="s-v">Level-3 Cycle-Accurate Verilator &amp; Spike Co-Sim</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="dossier-body">
        <p>
          Ara is a scalable, open-source vector coprocessor co-designed to accelerate high-performance scientific and machine learning workloads when coupled to the CVA6 64-bit application core. It features full compliance with the ratified RISC-V Vector Extension version 1.0. Ara's vector execution unit is physically partitioned into independent parallel lanes, each containing a dedicated integer ALU, a multi-precision floating-point unit (FP64/FP32/FP16), and eight single-port SRAM banks to prevent read conflicts during chained vector arithmetic.
        </p>
        <div class="dossier-pros-cons">
          <div class="pros-box">
            <strong>Key Strengths:</strong>
            <ul>
              <li>Silicon-proven 22FDX tapeout achieving &gt;1 GHz operating frequency.</li>
              <li>Element-wise chaining allows instructions to start executing before prior vector operands finish retiring.</li>
              <li>Integrated into the Cheshire SoC platform with full Linux driver support.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="cons-box">
            <strong>Key Limitations:</strong>
            <ul>
              <li>Requires an asynchronous coprocessor queue from an in-order host core (CVA6), leading to utilization drops on short vector reductions.</li>
              <li>Monolithic crossbar area scales as \(O(N^2)\) in 16-lane configurations.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dossier-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/pulp-platform/ara" target="_blank" class="core-link-pill">GitHub Repository</a>
          <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.00478" target="_blank" class="core-link-pill">IEEE TVLSI 2020 Paper</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DOSSIER 2: ARAXL -->
    <div id="core-araxl" class="core-dossier-card">
      <div class="dossier-header">
        <div class="dossier-badge-row">
          <span class="badge badge-blue">ARCHETYPE 4</span>
          <span class="badge badge-green">CLUSTERED RVV SCALE-UP</span>
          <span class="badge badge-yellow">DATE 2025</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="dossier-title">AraXL &bull; Clustered Multi-Bank VRF Vector Scale-Up</h3>
        <span class="dossier-sub">ETH Zurich &amp; Univ. of Bologna &bull; Solderpad-0.51 &bull; SystemVerilog</span>
      </div>

      <div class="dossier-specs-grid">
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">ISA:</span><span class="s-v">RV64GCV (Vector 1.0 Compliant)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Lanes:</span><span class="s-v">8 Lanes (Dual 4-Lane Clusters)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Vector Length:</span><span class="s-v">4096-bit (VLEN)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">VRF Architecture:</span><span class="s-v">Distributed Clustered Local Banks</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Memory Interface:</span><span class="s-v">Dual 256-bit AXI4 Ports (512-bit Aggregate)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Physical Area:</span><span class="s-v">~340 kGE (8 Lanes, 22FDX)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Clock Frequency:</span><span class="s-v">1.15 GHz @ 0.8V (GF 22FDX)</span></div>
        <div class="spec-item"><span class="s-k">Measured GEMM:</span><span class="s-v">7.821 Ops/Cycle (97.76% Peak Saturation)</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="dossier-body">
        <p>
          AraXL addresses the physical synthesis and wire congestion bottlenecks of wide monolithic vector coprocessors. Rather than scaling a single unified crossbar across eight or sixteen lanes, AraXL partitions the execution lanes into autonomous 4-lane sub-clusters. Each sub-cluster integrates its own local VRF banking and independent 256-bit AXI4 memory port. A lightweight hierarchical bridge handles inter-cluster reductions, eliminating 73% of crossbar routing area while achieving a record 97.76% utilization on double-precision GEMM.
        </p>
        <div class="dossier-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/pulp-platform/ara" target="_blank" class="core-link-pill">GitHub Repository</a>
          <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.10301" target="_blank" class="core-link-pill">DATE 2025 Paper</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- DOSSIER 3: GEMMINI -->
    <div id="core-gemmini" class="core-dossier-card">
      <div class="dossier-header">
        <div class="dossier-badge-row">
          <span class="badge badge-yellow">ARCHETYPE 6</span>
          <span class="badge badge-coral">2D SPATIAL SYSTOLIC</span>
          <span class="badge badge-teal">TSMC 16nm TAPE-OUT</span>
